statement:
A license key `s` is made of letters, digits and dashes `'-'`; the dashes split it into groups, but those groups can have any sizes. Rewrite the key using integer `k`:

- drop every existing dash and turn each lowercase letter into uppercase;
- regroup the remaining characters from the right so every group has exactly `k` characters, except the first group, which may be shorter but is never empty;
- join consecutive groups with a single `'-'`.

Return the new key. If `s` has no letters or digits at all, return the empty string.

validator:
function validate([s, k]) {
  if (typeof s !== 'string' || s.length < 1 || s.length > 100000) return 's needs 1 to 100000 characters.';
  if (!/^[A-Za-z0-9-]+$/.test(s)) return 's may contain only letters, digits and dashes.';
  if (!Number.isInteger(k) || k < 1 || k > 10000) return 'k is an integer from 1 to 10000.';
  return null;
}

